<title>INDIA: India Mahindra Ugine 96/97 net rises.</title>
<headline>India Mahindra Ugine 96/97 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	   (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		110.33     vs	107.60</p>
<p>    Sales		   3,178.27     vs    2,669.51</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   2.0	vs	  2.0</p>
<p>    Other income	     60.06     vs	 41.87</p>
<p>    Expenditure	   2,874.47     vs    2,451.85</p>
<p>    Interest		  147.53     vs	 99.52</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    216.34     vs	159.99</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     89.66     vs	 53.50</p>
<p>    Tax			  16.34     vs	 Nil</p>
<p>Note - Mahindra Ugine Steel Company Ltd makes value-added steel products. It is part of the Mahindra and Mahindra industrial group.</p>
<p>It said the acquisition in March 1996 a stampings unit which supplies pressed steel components for the automotive sector helped boost operations. The alloy steel industry faced problems of oversupply and sluggish demand, the firm said.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
